## Security Considerations

### Secret Handling

**Never log secrets**:
```rust
use secret_rs::Secret;

#[derive(Config)]
struct Settings {
    #[config(secret)]
    database_password: Secret<String>,
}

// Debug implementation shows [REDACTED]
println!("{:?}", settings.database_password);  // [REDACTED]
```

---

### Input Validation

**Validate all input**:
```rust
#[derive(Config)]
struct Settings {
    #[config(url)]
    api_endpoint: String,  // Validated URL

    #[config(email)]
    admin_email: String,  // Validated email

    #[config(non_empty)]
    app_name: String,  // Non-empty string
}
```

---

### File Permissions

**Check file permissions**:
```rust
use std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;

fn load_config_secure(path: &str) -> Result<Settings> {
    let metadata = fs::metadata(path)?;
    let permissions = metadata.permissions();
    let mode = permissions.mode();

    // Check file is not world-readable
    if mode & 0o044 != 0 {
        return Err(Error::security(
            "Config file is world-readable. Use chmod 600."
        ));
    }

    Settings::load_from_file(path)
}
```

---

### Code Execution Prevention

**Disable arbitrary code execution**:
```rust
// NEVER do this:
// eval(config["script"]);  // Dangerous!

// Instead, use safe alternatives:
#[derive(Config)]
struct Settings {
    #[config(non_empty)]
    script_name: String,  // Whitelist allowed scripts
}
```

