## Running Validations

### Validating Files

#### CSV Files

```rust
let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .validate_csv("users.csv")?;
```

#### Parquet Files

```rust
let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .validate_parquet("users.parquet")?;
```

#### JSON Files

```rust
let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .validate_json("users.json")?;
```

### Validating Polars DataFrames

```rust
use polars::prelude::*;

let df = CsvReader::from_path("users.csv")?
    .has_header(true)
    .finish()?;

let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .expect(unique("id"))
    .validate(&df)?;
```

### Validating SQL Databases

```rust
use dataval::SqlAdapter;

let adapter = PostgresAdapter::connect("postgresql://localhost/mydb")?;

let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .expect(unique("id"))
    .validate_sql(&adapter, "users")?;
```

### Parallel Validation

```rust
let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("col1"))
    .expect(no_nulls("col2"))
    .expect(no_nulls("col3"))
    // ... 100 more expectations
    .parallel(true)  // Run all in parallel (default)
    .validate(&df)?;
```

### Stop on First Error

```rust
let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .expect(unique("id"))
    .stop_on_first_error(true)  // Stop immediately on failure
    .validate(&df)?;
```

