## Profiling Data

### What is Profiling?

**Profiling** automatically analyzes your data to understand its structure, statistics, and patterns. Use profiling to:
- Understand your data
- Discover issues
- Get expectation suggestions

### Basic Profiling

```rust
use dataval::Profiler;

let profiler = Profiler::new();
let profile = profiler.profile_csv("users.csv")?;

println!("Rows: {}", profile.row_count);
println!("Columns: {}", profile.column_count);

for (name, col_profile) in &profile.columns {
    println!("  {}: {} nulls, {} unique values",
        name,
        col_profile.null_count,
        col_profile.unique_count
    );
}
```

**Output**:

```
Rows: 10000
Columns: 5
  id: 0 nulls, 10000 unique values
  name: 5 nulls, 9532 unique values
  email: 12 nulls, 9876 unique values
  age: 23 nulls, 65 unique values
  salary: 0 nulls, 8234 unique values
```

### Detailed Profiling

```rust
let profiler = Profiler::new()
    .statistics(true)
    .histograms(true)
    .correlations(true);

let profile = profiler.profile_csv("users.csv")?;

// Get column statistics
if let Some(stats) = profile.column("age").and_then(|c| c.statistics.as_ref()) {
    println!("Age Statistics:");
    println!("  Min: {}", stats.min.unwrap());
    println!("  Max: {}", stats.max.unwrap());
    println!("  Mean: {:.2}", stats.mean.unwrap());
    println!("  Median: {:.2}", stats.median.unwrap());
    println!("  StdDev: {:.2}", stats.stddev.unwrap());
}
```

### Suggesting Expectations

Let the profiler automatically suggest expectations:

```rust
let profiler = Profiler::new();
let suggestions = profiler.suggest_expectations_csv("users.csv")?;

for suggestion in suggestions {
    println!("{:.0}% - {}", suggestion.confidence * 100.0, suggestion.code_snippet);
    println!("     Reason: {}", suggestion.reason);
    println!();
}
```

**Output**:

```
100% - .expect(no_nulls("id"))
     Reason: Column has no null values

95% - .expect(unique("id"))
     Reason: Column appears to be a primary key (all unique values)

100% - .expect(in_range("age", 18..=80))
     Reason: Observed age range: 18 to 80

90% - .expect(is_email("email"))
     Reason: Column name and pattern match email format
```

### Using Suggestions

```rust
let profiler = Profiler::new();
let suggestions = profiler.suggest_expectations_csv("users.csv")?;

// Filter high-confidence suggestions
let high_confidence: Vec<_> = suggestions
    .into_iter()
    .filter(|s| s.confidence >= 0.9)
    .collect();

println!("Suggested Validator:");
println!("let validator = Validator::new()");
for suggestion in &high_confidence {
    println!("    {}", suggestion.code_snippet);
}
```

### Sampled Profiling

For large datasets, profile a sample:

```rust
let profiler = Profiler::new()
    .sample_size(10000);  // Profile 10,000 rows

let profile = profiler.profile_csv("huge_dataset.csv")?;
```

