## Setting Up Alerts

### Why Alerts?

Alerts notify you immediately when data quality issues occur. Set up alerts to:
- Get notified in Slack
- Receive email alerts
- Trigger PagerDuty incidents
- Call custom webhooks

### Slack Alerts

```rust
use dataval::alert::SlackAlert;

let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .on_failure(
        SlackAlert::new("#data-quality")
            .webhook_url(std::env::var("SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL")?)
    )
    .validate_csv("users.csv")?;
```

**Slack Message Example**:

```
⚠️ Data Quality Alert

Data Source: users.csv
Quality Score: 85.7% (6/7 expectations passed)

Failed Expectations:
  ✗ no_nulls("email")
    Expected: 0 nulls
    Actual: 23 nulls (0.23%)

View full report: /path/to/report.html
```

### Conditional Alerts

Only alert when quality score is below threshold:

```rust
SlackAlert::new("#data-quality")
    .on_quality_score_below(95.0)  // Only alert if score < 95%
```

### Email Alerts

```rust
use dataval::alert::EmailAlert;

let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .on_failure(
        EmailAlert::new(vec!["data-team@example.com"])
            .subject("Data Quality Alert: users.csv")
            .smtp_server("smtp.gmail.com")
    )
    .validate_csv("users.csv")?;
```

### PagerDuty Alerts

```rust
use dataval::alert::PagerDutyAlert;

let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .on_failure(
        PagerDutyAlert::new(std::env::var("PAGERDUTY_KEY")?)
            .severity(Severity::Error)
    )
    .validate_csv("users.csv")?;
```

### Webhook Alerts

```rust
use dataval::alert::WebhookAlert;

let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .on_failure(
        WebhookAlert::new("https://api.example.com/alerts")
            .header("Authorization", "Bearer token123")
    )
    .validate_csv("users.csv")?;
```

### Multiple Alerts

```rust
use dataval::alert::{CompositeAlert, SlackAlert, EmailAlert};

let alert = CompositeAlert::new()
    .add(Box::new(SlackAlert::new("#data-quality")))
    .add(Box::new(EmailAlert::new(vec!["team@example.com"])));

let report = Validator::new()
    .expect(no_nulls("id"))
    .on_failure(alert)
    .validate_csv("users.csv")?;
```

