## Data Quality Monitoring

### Use Case: Continuous Data Quality Monitoring

Monitor data quality in production systems and get alerted on issues.

#### Architecture

```
┌─────────────┐
│ Data Source │ (CSV, Database, API, Stream)
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐
│  Scheduled Validation   │ (cron, Airflow, etc.)
└──────┬──────────────────┘
       │
       ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐
│  dataval-rs Validator   │
└──────┬──────────────────┘
       │
       ├─→ Success ─→ Log to metrics
       │
       └─→ Failure ─→ Alert + Log
```

#### Implementation

```rust
use dataval::{Validator, Profiler, expectations::column::*};
use std::time::Duration;
use tokio::time::interval;

struct DataQualityMonitor {
    validators: HashMap<String, Validator>,
    alert_handlers: Vec<Box<dyn AlertHandler>>,
}

impl DataQualityMonitor {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            validators: HashMap::new(),
            alert_handlers: vec![
                Box::new(SlackAlert::new("#data-quality")),
                Box::new(EmailAlert::new(vec!["team@example.com"])),
            ],
        }
    }

    pub fn add_dataset(&mut self, name: String, validator: Validator) {
        self.validators.insert(name, validator);
    }

    pub async fn start_monitoring(&self, interval_secs: u64) {
        let mut interval = interval(Duration::from_secs(interval_secs));

        loop {
            interval.tick().await;

            for (name, validator) in &self.validators {
                self.monitor_dataset(name, validator).await;
            }
        }
    }

    async fn monitor_dataset(&self, name: &str, validator: &Validator) {
        println!("Monitoring dataset: {}", name);

        let data_path = format!("data/{}.csv", name);

        match validator.validate_csv(&data_path) {
            Ok(report) => {
                if !report.passed() {
                    // Send alerts
                    for handler in &self.alert_handlers {
                        let _ = handler.send(&report);
                    }
                }

                // Log quality score
                metrics::gauge!(
                    "data_quality_score",
                    report.quality_score(),
                    "dataset" => name
                );
            },
            Err(e) => {
                eprintln!("Validation error for {}: {}", name, e);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

#### Monitoring Dashboard

Track quality metrics over time:

```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;

struct QualityTracker {
    history: HashMap<String, Vec<QualitySnapshot>>,
}

struct QualitySnapshot {
    timestamp: DateTime<Utc>,
    quality_score: f64,
    failed_expectations: Vec<String>,
    row_count: usize,
}

impl QualityTracker {
    pub fn record_validation(&mut self, dataset: &str, report: &ValidationReport) {
        let snapshot = QualitySnapshot {
            timestamp: Utc::now(),
            quality_score: report.quality_score(),
            failed_expectations: report.failures()
                .into_iter()
                .map(|f| f.expectation_name.clone())
                .collect(),
            row_count: report.row_count,
        };

        self.history
            .entry(dataset.to_string())
            .or_default()
            .push(snapshot);
    }

    pub fn get_trend(&self, dataset: &str, window_hours: i64) -> Option<QualityTrend> {
        let snapshots = self.history.get(dataset)?;

        let cutoff = Utc::now() - Duration::hours(window_hours);
        let recent: Vec<_> = snapshots
            .iter()
            .filter(|s| s.timestamp > cutoff)
            .collect();

        if recent.is_empty() {
            return None;
        }

        let avg_score = recent.iter()
            .map(|s| s.quality_score)
            .sum::<f64>() / recent.len() as f64;

        let min_score = recent.iter()
            .map(|s| s.quality_score)
            .fold(f64::INFINITY, f64::min);

        let max_score = recent.iter()
            .map(|s| s.quality_score)
            .fold(f64::NEG_INFINITY, f64::max);

        Some(QualityTrend {
            dataset: dataset.to_string(),
            window_hours,
            avg_score,
            min_score,
            max_score,
            snapshots_count: recent.len(),
        })
    }
}
