## Architecture Overview

### System Layers

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              API Layer (Public)                     │
│  Database, Collection, Document, Query, Index       │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                        │
                        ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Query Engine                           │
│  Parser, Optimizer, Planner                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                        │
                        ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Execution Layer                        │
│  AggregationPipeline, IndexManager, Cursor          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                        │
                        ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Storage Backend Layer                  │
│  StorageBackend trait (SQLite, Sled, Memory)        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Key Traits

**StorageBackend:**
```rust
pub trait StorageBackend: Send + Sync {
    fn create_collection(&self, name: &str) -> Result<()>;
    fn insert(&self, collection: &str, doc: &Document) -> Result<ObjectId>;
    fn find(&self, collection: &str, query: &Query) -> Result<Vec<Document>>;
    fn update(&self, collection: &str, query: &Query, update: &Document) -> Result<u64>;
    fn delete(&self, collection: &str, query: &Query) -> Result<u64>;
    // ... more methods
}
```

**PipelineStage:**
```rust
pub trait PipelineStage: Send + Sync {
    fn execute(&self, docs: Vec<Document>) -> Result<Vec<Document>>;
}
```

### Data Flow

**Insert Operation:**
```
1. Application calls users.insert_one(doc)
2. Collection validates document
3. Collection generates ObjectId if needed
4. Collection calls backend.insert()
5. Backend stores document (SQLite/Sled/Memory)
6. IndexManager indexes document
7. Collection returns ObjectId to application
```

**Find Operation:**
```
1. Application calls users.find(query)
2. Collection creates Query object
3. IndexManager finds best index
4. If index exists: backend.find_with_index()
5. Else: backend.find_with_scan()
6. Backend returns matching documents
7. Collection applies projection, sort, limit, skip
8. Collection returns results to application
```

