## Performance Tuning

### 1. Producer Tuning

```rust
// High throughput
let producer = Producer::builder()
    .batch_size(100_000)     // Larger batches
    .linger(Duration::from_millis(100))  // Wait longer
    .compression(Compression::Zstd)  // Compress
    .buffer_memory(64 * 1024 * 1024)  // 64MB buffer
    .build()?;

// Low latency
let producer = Producer::builder()
    .batch_size(16 * 1024)    // Smaller batches
    .linger(Duration::from_millis(0))  // No waiting
    .compression(Compression::None)  // No compression
    .build()?;
```

### 2. Consumer Tuning

```rust
// High throughput
let consumer = Consumer::builder()
    .fetch_min_bytes(1024 * 1024)  // 1MB minimum
    .fetch_max_wait_ms(1000)  // Wait up to 1s
    .max_poll_records(1000)  // More records
    .build()?;

// Low latency
let consumer = Consumer::builder()
    .fetch_min_bytes(1)  // As little as possible
    .fetch_max_wait_ms(100)  // Wait 100ms max
    .max_poll_records(100)  // Fewer records
    .build()?;
```

### 3. Storage Tuning

```rust
// High throughput
let config = StorageConfig {
    segment_bytes: 1_000_000_000,  // 1GB segments
    flush_messages: 100_000,  // Flush less often
    flush_ms: 10_000,  // Flush every 10s
};

// Low latency
let config = StorageConfig {
    segment_bytes: 100_000_000,  // 100MB segments
    flush_messages: 1000,  // Flush frequently
    flush_ms: 100,  // Flush every 100ms
};
```

### 4. Compression Trade-offs

| Codec | Ratio | Speed | Use Case |
|-------|-------|-------|----------|
| None | 1.0x | Fastest | Low CPU, small events |
| Lz4 | 2.0x | Fast | Balanced |
| Snappy | 2.5x | Faster | Good default |
| Zstd | 3.0x | Medium | Best compression |
| Gzip | 3.5x | Slow | Max compression |

### 5. Benchmarking

```bash
# Run benchmarks
cargo bench

# Compare implementations
cargo bench --bench producer -- --baseline main

# Generate flamegraph
cargo install flamegraph
cargo flamegraph --example producer
```

## Performance Optimization Tips

### 1. Use Zero-Copy Reads

```rust
// Instead of copying
let record = log.read(offset).await?;
let bytes = record.value.clone();  // Copy

// Use zero-copy
let record = log.read(offset).await?;
let bytes = &record.value;  // Reference
```

### 2. Reuse Buffers

```rust
// Instead of allocating each time
for event in events {
    let buffer = Vec::new();  // Allocates
    process(event, &mut buffer)?;
}

// Reuse buffer
let mut buffer = Vec::with_capacity(1024);
for event in events {
    buffer.clear();
    process(event, &mut buffer)?;
}
```

### 3. Batch Operations

```rust
// Instead of individual writes
for event in events {
    log.append(event).await?;  // Slow
}

// Batch writes
log.append_batch(events).await?;  // Fast
```

### 4. Use Async Effectively

```rust
// Instead of sequential
for event in events {
    process(event).await?;  // Sequential
}

// Process concurrently
let handles: Vec<_> = events
    .into_iter()
    .map(|e| tokio::spawn(process(e)))
    .collect();

for handle in handles {
    handle.await??;
}
```

