## Best Practices

### 1. Key Design

**DO:**
```rust
// Descriptive, namespaced
"user:{id}"
"session:{token}"
"cache:query:{hash}"
"ratelimit:{user_id}"
"events:user:{id}"
```

**DON'T:**
```rust
// Too short
"x"
"k"

// No structure
"user123alice"
"session_abc_123_2024"

// Missing ID
"user_data"
"session_info"
```

### 2. TTL Management

**DO:**
```rust
// Set TTL on temporary data
cache.set_with_options("session:abc", &data, SetOptions {
    ttl: Some(Duration::from_secs(1800)), // 30 min
    ..Default::default()
}).await?;

// Use reasonable defaults
cache.set_with_options("cache:query", &result, SetOptions {
    ttl: Some(Duration::from_secs(300)), // 5 min
    ..Default::default()
}).await?;
```

**DON'T:**
```rust
// No TTL on temporary data (memory leak!)
cache.set("session:abc", &data).await?;

// Too short (cache ineffective)
cache.set_with_options("cache:query", &result, SetOptions {
    ttl: Some(Duration::from_secs(1)), // 1 second!
    ..Default::default()
}).await?;
```

### 3. Error Handling

**DO:**
```rust
// Handle errors gracefully
match cache.get("key").await {
    Ok(Some(value)) => { /* use value */ },
    Ok(None) => { /* handle cache miss */ },
    Err(Error::Timeout(_)) => { /* fallback to DB */ },
    Err(e) => { eprintln!("Cache error: {}", e); /* fallback */ },
}
```

**DON'T:**
```rust
// Panic on error
let value = cache.get("key").await?.unwrap();

// Ignore errors
let _ = cache.set("key", "value").await; // Error lost!
```

### 4. Serialization

**DO:**
```rust
use serde::{Serialize, Deserialize};

#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]
struct User {
    id: u64,
    name: String,
}

// Serialize automatically
cache.set("user:123", &user).await?;
let user: User = cache.get("user:123").await?.unwrap();
```

**DON'T:**
```rust
// Manual serialization (error-prone)
let json = serde_json::to_string(&user)?;
cache.set("user:123", json.as_bytes()).await?;

let bytes = cache.get("user:123").await?.unwrap();
let user: User = serde_json::from_slice(&bytes)?;
```

### 5. Connection Management

**DO:**
```rust
// Reuse connection
let cache = Cache::connect("redis://localhost:6379").await?;

// Pass to functions
async fn get_user(cache: &Cache, id: u64) -> Result<Option<User>> {
    cache.get(&format!("user:{}", id)).await
}
```

**DON'T:**
```rust
// New connection per request (slow!)
async fn get_user(id: u64) -> Result<Option<User>> {
    let cache = Cache::connect("redis://localhost:6379").await?;
    cache.get(&format!("user:{}", id)).await
}
```

