## Performance Tips

### 1. Use Batch Operations

```rust
// DON'T: Individual calls
for id in user_ids {
    let user: Option<User> = cache.get(&format!("user:{}", id)).await?;
}

// DO: Batch get
let keys: Vec<_> = user_ids.iter().map(|id| format!("user:{}", id)).collect();
let users: Vec<Option<User>> = cache.mget(&keys).await?;
```

### 2. Pipeline Commands

```rust
// DON'T: Sequential
cache.set("key1", "value1").await?;
cache.set("key2", "value2").await?;
cache.set("key3", "value3").await?;

// DO: Pipeline
let commands = vec![
    Command::Set("key1", "value1"),
    Command::Set("key2", "value2"),
    Command::Set("key3", "value3"),
];
cache.pipeline(commands).await?;
```

### 3. Monitor Hit Rate

```rust
let metrics = cache.metrics().await?;
println!("Hit rate: {:.2}%", metrics.hit_rate * 100.0);

// Aim for > 80% hit rate
if metrics.hit_rate < 0.8 {
    eprintln!("Warning: Low cache hit rate!");
}
```

### 4. Use Appropriate TTL

```rust
// Too short = cache misses
// Too long = stale data

// Good balance
cache.set_with_options("user:123", &user, SetOptions {
    ttl: Some(Duration::from_secs(600)), // 10 min
    ..Default::default()
}).await?;
```

