## Adding Custom Metric Types

### Example: Adding a "Set" Metric

**Goal**: Track unique cardinalities (e.g., unique users).

### Step 1: Define Metric Type

Create `src/set.rs`:

```rust
use std::collections::HashSet;
use std::sync::{Arc, RwLock};
use std::hash::Hash;

pub struct Set<T: Hash + Eq> {
    name: Arc<str>,
    labels: Labels,
    values: RwLock<HashSet<T>>,
    help: Arc<str>,
}

impl<T: Hash + Eq> Set<T> {
    /// Create a new Set builder.
    pub fn new(name: impl Into<Arc<str>>) -> SetBuilder<T> {
        SetBuilder {
            name: name.into(),
            help: Arc::from(""),
            labels: Vec::new(),
            registry: None,
        }
    }

    /// Add a value to the set.
    pub fn insert(&self, value: T) -> bool {
        let mut values = self.values.write().unwrap();
        values.insert(value)
    }

    /// Get the current cardinality.
    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {
        let values = self.values.read().unwrap();
        values.len()
    }

    /// Clear the set.
    pub fn clear(&self) {
        let mut values = self.values.write().unwrap();
        values.clear();
    }
}
```

### Step 2: Create Builder

```rust
pub struct SetBuilder<T: Hash + Eq> {
    name: Arc<str>,
    help: Arc<str>,
    labels: Vec<(String, String)>,
    registry: Option<Registry>,
}

impl<T: Hash + Eq> SetBuilder<T> {
    pub fn label(mut self, key: impl Into<String>, value: impl Into<String>) -> Self {
        self.labels.push((key.into(), value.into()));
        self
    }

    pub fn help(mut self, help: impl Into<Arc<str>>) -> Self {
        self.help = help.into();
        self
    }

    pub fn registry(mut self, registry: Registry) -> Self {
        self.registry = Some(registry);
        self
    }

    pub fn build(self) -> Arc<Set<T>> {
        let registry = self.registry.unwrap_or_else(|| Registry::global());
        let labels = Labels::from_builder(self.labels);

        let set = Arc::new(Set {
            name: self.name,
            labels,
            values: RwLock::new(HashSet::new()),
            help: self.help,
        });

        registry.register(Metric::Set(set.clone())).unwrap();
        set
    }
}
```

### Step 3: Integrate with Registry

Update `src/registry.rs`:

```rust
pub enum Metric {
    Counter(Arc<Counter>),
    Gauge(Arc<Gauge>),
    Histogram(Arc<Histogram>),
    Summary(Arc<Summary>),
    Set(Arc<dyn Any + Send + Sync>), // Custom metric
}
```

### Step 4: Implement Prometheus Formatting

Add `to_prometheus_format` method:

```rust
impl<T: Hash + Eq + Display> Set<T> {
    pub fn to_prometheus_format(&self) -> String {
        let values = self.values.read().unwrap();
        let cardinality = values.len();

        format!(
            "{}{} {}",
            self.name,
            self.labels.to_prometheus_format(),
            cardinality
        )
    }
}
```

### Step 5: Write Tests

Create `tests/set_test.rs`:

```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn test_set_insert() {
        let set = Set::new("unique_users").build();

        assert_eq!(set.len(), 0);
        assert!(set.insert("alice"));
        assert_eq!(set.len(), 1);
        assert!(!set.insert("alice")); // Duplicate
        assert_eq!(set.len(), 1);
        assert!(set.insert("bob"));
        assert_eq!(set.len(), 2);
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_set_clear() {
        let set = Set::new("unique_users").build();

        set.insert("alice");
        set.insert("bob");
        assert_eq!(set.len(), 2);

        set.clear();
        assert_eq!(set.len(), 0);
    }
}
```

### Step 6: Add Benchmark

Create `benches/set.rs`:

```rust
use criterion::{black_box, criterion_group, criterion_main, Criterion};

fn bench_set_insert(c: &mut Criterion) {
    let set = Set::new("bench_set").build();

    c.bench_function("set_insert", |b| {
