## Performance Tuning

### Target Performance

| Operation | Target | Notes |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| Counter::inc() | <10ns | Atomic fetch_add |
| Gauge::set() | <10ns | Atomic store |
| Histogram::observe() | <100ns | Binary search + increment |
| Registry::scrape() (10K metrics) | <10ms | Pre-allocated buffer |

---

### Optimization Techniques

#### 1. Use Atomic Operations

```rust
// ✅ Good: Lock-free
struct Counter {
    value: AtomicU64,
}

// ❌ Bad: Mutex (slow)
struct Counter {
    value: Mutex<u64>,
}
```

#### 2. Pre-allocate Memory

```rust
// ✅ Good: Pre-allocate 1MB
let mut output = String::with_capacity(1024 * 1024);

// ❌ Bad: Reallocation during scrape
let mut output = String::new();
```

#### 3. Sort Once

```rust
// ✅ Good: Sort at registration
let mut labels = labels;
labels.sort_by_key(|(k, _)| k);

// ❌ Bad: Sort on every scrape
labels.sort(); // O(n log n) on every scrape
```

#### 4. Use Arc for Shared Strings

```rust
// ✅ Good: Shared ownership
pub struct Counter {
    name: Arc<str>, // No copy
}

// ❌ Bad: Owned String
pub struct Counter {
    name: String, // Copied for every clone
}
```

