## Code Style

### Naming Conventions

**Types**: PascalCase
```rust
pub struct Counter { }
pub enum Metric { }
```

**Functions**: snake_case
```rust
pub fn inc(&self) { }
pub fn observe(&self, value: f64) { }
```

**Constants**: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE
```rust
pub const DEFAULT_BUCKETS: [f64; 11] = [...];
```

---

### Documentation Comments

**Public APIs**: Must have documentation

```rust
/// Increment the counter by 1.
///
/// # Performance
///
/// ~10ns (single atomic fetch_add)
///
/// # Examples
///
/// ```
/// let counter = Counter::new("requests_total").build();
/// counter.inc();
/// ```
pub fn inc(&self) {
    self.value.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
}
```

---

### Error Handling

**Use Result<T, E> for fallible operations**:

```rust
pub fn register(&self, metric: Metric) -> Result<(), RegistrationError> {
    if self.contains(&metric) {
        return Err(RegistrationError::Duplicate);
    }
    self.insert(metric);
    Ok(())
}
```

**Use thiserror for error types**:

```rust
use thiserror::Error;

#[derive(Debug, Error)]
pub enum RegistrationError {
    #[error("Metric \"{name}\" already exists")]
    Duplicate { name: String },

    #[error("Invalid metric name: {0}")]
    InvalidName(String),
}
```

---

### Thread Safety

**Use Arc for shared ownership**:

```rust
pub struct Counter {
    value: AtomicU64,
}

let counter = Arc::new(Counter::new("test").build());
std::thread::spawn(move || {
    counter.inc();
});
```

**Use RwLock for read-mostly data**:

```rust
pub struct Registry {
    metrics: RwLock<HashMap<String, Metric>>,
}
```

