## Architecture Deep Dive

### Core Components

```
profiler-rs/
├── src/
│   ├── lib.rs              # Public API
│   ├── profiler.rs         # Profiler implementation
│   ├── sampler.rs          # Platform-specific sampling
│   ├── unwinder.rs         # Stack unwinding
│   ├── transformer.rs      # Profile construction
│   ├── analyzer.rs         # Analysis engine
│   ├── renderer.rs         # Visualization
│   ├── exporter.rs         # Export formats
│   └── platform/
│       ├── linux.rs        # Linux perf_events
│       ├── macos.rs        # macOS kdebug
│       └── windows.rs      # Windows ETW
```

### Data Flow

```
1. Application starts
   ↓
2. Profiler::start()
   ↓
3. Sampler starts (platform-specific)
   ↓
4. Timer triggers every N ms
   ↓
5. Sampler captures IP (instruction pointer)
   ↓
6. Unwinder walks stack → Vec<StackFrame>
   ↓
7. Transformer aggregates samples
   ↓
8. Profiler::stop() → Profile
   ↓
9. Analyzer generates insights
   ↓
10. Renderer produces visualization
```

### Key Data Structures

#### Raw Sample

```rust
pub struct RawSample {
    pub timestamp: Instant,
    pub ip: usize,              // Instruction pointer
    pub sp: usize,              // Stack pointer
    pub bp: usize,              // Base pointer
    pub thread_id: ThreadId,
    pub cpu_id: Option<u32>,
}
```

#### Stack Frame

```rust
pub struct StackFrame {
    pub ip: usize,
    pub function_name: Option<String>,
    pub module_name: Option<String>,
    pub file: Option<String>,
    pub line: Option<u32>,
    pub inlined: bool,
}
```

#### Profile

```rust
pub struct Profile {
    pub samples: Vec<Sample>,
    pub call_graph: CallGraph,
    pub metadata: ProfileMetadata,
}
```

