## Memory Leak Detection

### Use Case: Growing Memory Usage

**Problem**: Memory usage increases over time

**Solution**: Memory profiling with leak detection

```rust
use profiler::{Profiler, ProfileType, MemoryLeakDetector};

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let profiler = Profiler::with_config(
        Config::builder()
            .profile_type(ProfileType::Memory)
            .continuous()
            .build()
    )?;

    run_application();

    let profile = profiler.stop()?;

    // Detect memory leaks
    if let Some(leak) = MemoryLeakDetector::detect(&profile) {
        eprintln!("Memory leak detected in {}!", leak.function);
        eprintln!("Leaking {} MB/sec", leak.rate);

        // Show allocation sites
        for site in leak.allocation_sites() {
            eprintln!("  Allocated at: {}", site);
        }
    }

    Ok(())
}
```

### Use Case: Cyclic References

**Problem**: Rc<RefCell>> cycles causing memory leaks

**Solution**: Profile and fix cycles

```rust
use std::rc::Rc;
use std::cell::RefCell;
use profiler::profile;

struct Node {
    data: String,
    next: Option<Rc<RefCell<Node>>>,
}

#[profile]
fn create_cycle() {
    let a = Rc::new(RefCell::new(Node {
        data: "A".to_string(),
        next: None,
    }));

    let b = Rc::new(RefCell::new(Node {
        data: "B".to_string(),
        next: Some(a.clone()),
    }));

    // Create cycle
    a.borrow_mut().next = Some(b);

    // Both A and B will never be deallocated!
}

// Fix: Use Weak instead
use std::rc::Weak;

struct NodeFixed {
    data: String,
    next: Option<Rc<RefCell<NodeFixed>>>,
    prev: Option<Weak<RefCell<NodeFixed>>>,  // Weak reference
}
```

**Results**:
- Memory profiling shows `create_cycle` allocates but never deallocates
- Fix by using `Weak` references
- Profile confirms no more leaks

