### Use Case: Expensive Computation

**Problem**: Mathematical calculations are slow

**Solution**: Profile and use optimized libraries

```rust
use profiler::profile;

#[profile]
fn compute_statistics(data: &[f64]) -> Statistics {
    // Before: Manual implementation (slow)
    // let mean = data.iter().sum::<f64>() / data.len() as f64;
    // let variance = data.iter().map(|x| (x - mean).powi(2)).sum::<f64>() / data.len() as f64;

    // After: Use ndarray (optimized, SIMD)
    use ndarray::Array1;
    let arr = Array1::from(data.to_vec());
    let mean = arr.mean().unwrap();
    let variance = arr.var(0.0);

    Statistics { mean, variance }
}
```

**Results**:
- Profile shows computation bottleneck
- Use optimized library (ndarray)
- 4x speedup

