## Function-Level Performance

### Use Case: Compare Implementations

**Problem**: Which implementation is faster?

**Solution**: Profile and compare

```rust
use profiler::{profile, Profile};

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    // Profile implementation A
    let (result_a, profile_a) = profile(|| {
        implementation_a(test_data())
    });

    // Profile implementation B
    let (result_b, profile_b) = profile(|| {
        implementation_b(test_data())
    });

    // Compare
    let report = profile_b.compare(&profile_a);

    println!("Implementation A: {:?}", profile_a.duration());
    println!("Implementation B: {:?}", profile_b.duration());

    if !report.regressions.is_empty() {
        println!("B is slower!");
    } else {
        println!("B is faster!");
    }

    Ok(())
}
```

### Use Case: Micro-optimization

**Problem**: Hot function needs optimization

**Solution**: Profile, optimize, verify

```rust
use profiler::profile;

// Before: Slow version
#[inline(never)]
fn process_string_slow(s: &str) -> String {
    s.chars()
        .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric())
        .collect()
}

// After: Fast version
#[inline(never)]
#[profile]
fn process_string_fast(s: &str) -> String {
    let mut result = String::with_capacity(s.len());
    for c in s.chars() {
        if c.is_alphanumeric() {
            result.push(c);
        }
    }
    result
}

// Benchmark both
fn main() {
    let test_data = "a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h,i,j".repeat(1000);

    let (_, profile_slow) = profile(|| {
        for _ in 0..1000 {
            process_string_slow(&test_data);
        }
    });

    let (_, profile_fast) = profile(|| {
        for _ in 0..1000 {
            process_string_fast(&test_data);
        }
    });

    println!("Slow: {:?}", profile_slow.duration());
    println!("Fast: {:?}", profile_fast.duration());
}
```

