## Distributed Profiling

### Use Case: Microservices Architecture

**Problem**: Request slow, don't know which service is bottleneck

**Solution**: Distributed profiling with tracer-rs

```rust
use profiler::{Profiler, DistributedProfile};
use tracer::{TraceContext, propagate_trace};

#[profiler::profile]
async fn handle_request(ctx: &TraceContext) -> Result<Response> {
    // Profile this service
    let _span = profiler::span!("handle_request");

    // Call other services (trace propagates)
    let user_data = fetch_user(ctx).await?;
    let posts = fetch_posts(ctx, user_data.id).await?;

    Ok(Response { user_data, posts })
}

async fn fetch_user(ctx: &TraceContext) -> Result<User> {
    let _span = profiler::span_with_trace("fetch_user", ctx);

    // HTTP request with trace header
    let client = reqwest::Client::new();
    let response = client
        .get("http://user-service/user")
        .header("X-Trace-Id", ctx.trace_id())
        .send()
        .await?;

    Ok(response.json().await?)
}
```

**Results**:
- Each service profiles its code
- Trace ID correlates profiles across services
- Identify which service is bottleneck

### Use Case: Aggregate Profiles

**Problem**: Multiple instances, need aggregate profile

**Solution**: Merge profiles from all instances

```bash
# On each instance
profiler run --output=instance1.prof -- ./my_app
profiler run --output=instance2.prof -- ./my_app
profiler run --output=instance3.prof -- ./my_app

# Merge all profiles
profiler merge instance*.prof --output=aggregate.prof

# Analyze aggregate
profiler report aggregate.prof
profiler flamegraph aggregate.prof
```

