## CI/CD Integration

### Use Case: Performance Regression Detection

**Problem**: Pull request introduces performance regression

**Solution**: Automated profiling in CI

```yaml
# .github/workflows/profile.yml
name: Performance Tests

on: [pull_request]

jobs:
  profile:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v2

      - name: Install profiler
        run: cargo install profiler-cli

      - name: Run benchmarks
        run: |
          profiler run --output=pr.prof -- cargo test --release

      - name: Compare with main
        run: |
          git checkout main
          profiler run --output=baseline.prof -- cargo test --release
          git checkout ${{ github.sha }}

      - name: Check for regressions
        run: |
          profiler compare baseline.prof pr.prof --fail-on-regression

      - name: Upload profile
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v2
        with:
          name: profile
          path: pr.prof
```

### Use Case: Performance Dashboard

**Problem**: Track performance over time

**Solution**: Continuous profiling and metrics

```rust
use profiler::{Profiler, ContinuousProfiler};
use metrics::{histogram, gauge};

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let profiler = ContinuousProfiler::start()?;

    run_application();

    let profile = profiler.stop()?;

    // Export metrics
    for hot_path in profile.hot_paths(5.0) {
        gauge!("hot_path_time", hot_path.total_time.as_millis() as f64,
            "function" => hot_path.function.clone()
        );
    }

    // Save profile for analysis
    profile.save_to_file("continuous.prof")?;

    Ok(())
}
```

