## Quick Start

### Installation

Add to your `Cargo.toml`:

```toml
[dependencies]
profiler = "0.1"
```

### Your First Profile

**1. Simple function profiling:**

```rust
use profiler::profile;

fn fibonacci(n: u64) -> u64 {
    if n <= 1 { n } else { fibonacci(n-1) + fibonacci(n-2) }
}

fn main() {
    let (result, profile) = profile(|| fibonacci(40));

    println!("Result: {}", result);
    println!("Duration: {:?}", profile.duration());
}
```

**2. Attribute-based profiling:**

```rust
use profiler::profile;

#[profile]
fn expensive_function() -> String {
    // Automatically profiled
    do_work()
}
```

**3. Manual control:**

```rust
use profiler::Profiler;

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let profiler = Profiler::start()?;

    // Your application runs
    run_application();

    let profile = profiler.stop()?;
    profile.save_to_file("app.prof")?;

    Ok(())
}
```

**4. CLI profiling (no code changes):**

```bash
# Profile any command
profiler run -- cargo run --release

# Generate flame chart
profiler flamegraph profile.prof --open

# Compare profiles
profiler compare baseline.prof current.prof
```

