## Example 1: Hello State Machine

**The simplest possible state machine**

```rust
use statemachine::{StateMachine, State, Event, Transitionable, TransitionError};

// Define states
struct On;
struct Off;

impl State for On {
    type Data = ();
    type Parent = ();
}

impl State for Off {
    type Data = ();
    type Parent = ();
}

// Define events
struct Toggle;
impl Event for Toggle {}

// Define transitions
impl Transitionable<Toggle> for Off {
    type Next = On;

    fn transition(self, _event: Toggle) -> Result<StateMachine<On>, TransitionError> {
        println!("💡 Turning on...");
        Ok(StateMachine::new())
    }
}

impl Transitionable<Toggle> for On {
    type Next = Off;

    fn transition(self, _event: Toggle) -> Result<StateMachine<Off>, TransitionError> {
        println!("🌑 Turning off...");
        Ok(StateMachine::new())
    }
}

fn main() {
    println!("=== Hello State Machine ===\n");

    let mut switch = StateMachine::<Off>::new();
    println!("Initial state: {}\n", switch.state_name());

    // Toggle on
    switch = switch.transition(Toggle).unwrap();
    println!("Current state: {}\n", switch.state_name());

    // Toggle off
    switch = switch.transition(Toggle).unwrap();
    println!("Current state: {}\n", switch.state_name());

    // Generate diagram
    println!("Generating diagram...");
    switch.write_diagram("hello.puml", DiagramFormat::PlantUML).unwrap();
    println!("✅ Diagram saved to hello.puml");
}
```

**Output**:

```
=== Hello State Machine ===

Initial state: Off

💡 Turning on...
Current state: On

🌑 Turning off...
Current state: Off

Generating diagram...
✅ Diagram saved to hello.puml
```

**Generated Diagram** (hello.puml):

```plantuml
@startuml
state Off {
  [*] --> Off
  Off --> On : Toggle
}
state On {
  On --> Off : Toggle
}
@enduml
```

