## Test Doubles

### Mocks

Mock objects verify behavior:

```rust
#[test]
fn test_with_mock() {
    let mut mock_db = auto_mock!(Database);

    mock_db
        .expect_get_user(eq(1))
        .returns(User { id: 1, name: "Alice" })
        .times(1);

    let service = UserService::new(mock_db);

    expect(service.get_user(1).name).to_equal("Alice");

    mock_db.verify();
}
```

### Stubs

Stubs provide canned responses:

```rust
struct StubUserService;

impl UserService for StubUserService {
    fn get_user(&self, id: i32) -> Option<User> {
        Some(User {
            id,
            name: "Stub User".to_string(),
        })
    }
}

#[test]
fn test_with_stub() {
    let service = StubUserService;
    expect(service.get_user(1).name).to_equal("Stub User");
}
```

### Fakes

Fakes have working implementations but use shortcuts:

```rust
struct FakeDatabase {
    users: HashMap<i32, User>,
}

impl FakeDatabase {
    fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            users: HashMap::new(),
        }
    }
}

impl Database for FakeDatabase {
    fn get_user(&self, id: i32) -> Option<User> {
        self.users.get(&id).cloned()
    }

    fn save_user(&mut self, user: User) -> Result<(), Error> {
        self.users.insert(user.id, user);
        Ok(())
    }
}

#[test]
fn test_with_fake() {
    let mut db = FakeDatabase::new();
    db.save_user(User { id: 1, name: "Alice".to_string() });

    expect(db.get_user(1)).to_be_some();
}
```

### Spies

Spies record calls for verification:

```rust
struct SpyUserService {
    inner: UserService,
    calls: Arc<Mutex<Vec<Call>>>,
}

impl SpyUserService {
    fn spy(inner: UserService) -> Self {
        Self {
            inner,
            calls: Arc::new(Mutex::new(Vec::new())),
        }
    }

    fn get_calls(&self) -> Vec<Call> {
        self.calls.lock().unwrap().clone()
    }
}

#[test]
fn test_with_spy() {
    let real_service = UserService::new(Database::in_memory());
    let spy = SpyUserService::spy(real_service);

    spy.get_user(1);

    expect(spy.get_calls()).to_have_length(1);
    expect(spy.get_calls()[0].method).to_equal("get_user");
}
```

