### Adding a New Aggregation Function

**Step 1**: Add to `Aggregate` enum (src/query/aggregate.rs)
```rust
pub enum Aggregate {
    Mean,
    Sum,
    Min,
    Max,
    Count,
    Stddev,  // New!
    // ...
}
```

**Step 2**: Implement aggregation logic
```rust
impl Aggregate {
    pub fn compute(&self, values: &[FieldValue]) -> FieldValue {
        match self {
            Aggregate::Mean => {
                let sum: f64 = values.iter().map(|v| v.as_float().unwrap()).sum();
                FieldValue::Float(sum / values.len() as f64)
            }
            Aggregate::Stddev => {
                let mean: f64 = values.iter().map(|v| v.as_float().unwrap()).sum::<f64>()
                    / values.len() as f64;
                let variance = values.iter()
                    .map(|v| {
                        let diff = v.as_float().unwrap() - mean;
                        diff * diff
                    })
                    .sum::<f64>() / values.len() as f64;
                FieldValue::Float(variance.sqrt())
            }
            // ...
        }
    }
}
```

