## ✨ Why tui-rs?

**10x simpler than other TUI frameworks.**

```rust
use tui::prelude::*;

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    tui::run(|ui| {
        ui.label("Hello, World!");
        ui.button("Click me", || {
            println!("Clicked!");
        });
    })
}
```

**No complex setup. No boilerplate. Just beautiful UIs.**

---

## 🎯 Key Features

- **🚀 Immediate Mode** - Describe your UI naturally, no retained widget tree
- **⚡ Async-First** - Built-in async/await support for modern Rust
- **🎨 CSS-Like Styling** - Declarative styles with themes
- **📐 Smart Layouts** - Flexbox-inspired responsive layouts
- **🧩 Widget Library** - 20+ built-in widgets
- **🔍 Virtual Scrolling** - Handle millions of items efficiently
- **🧪 Testing Support** - Test your UIs with ease
- **🌍 Cross-Platform** - Linux, macOS, Windows

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

### Installation

Add to your `Cargo.toml`:

```toml
[dependencies]
tui-rs = "0.1"
```

### Your First App

```rust
use tui::prelude::*;

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let mut count = 0;

    tui::run(|ui| {
        ui.col(|ui| {
            ui.label("Counter App")
                .style(fg(Blue) + bold);

            ui.label(format!("Count: {}", count))
                .style(fg(Yellow));

            ui.row(|ui| {
                ui.button("-", || {
                    count -= 1;
                });

                ui.button("+", || {
                    count += 1;
                });
            });
        });
    })
}
```

That's it! Run with `cargo run`.

