### 3. Saga Transaction Model

**Architecture**:
```
Saga Orchestrator
    │
    ├──► Step 1 (Action)
    │       └─► Compensation 1
    ├──► Step 2 (Action)
    │       └─► Compensation 2
    └──► Step 3 (Action)
            └─► Compensation 3
```

**Saga Execution**:
```rust
pub struct Saga {
    id: SagaId,
    steps: Vec<SagaStep>,
    completed: Vec<CompletedStep>,
    state: SagaState,
}

impl Saga {
    pub async fn execute(mut self) -> Result<SagaResult> {
        self.state = SagaState::InProgress;

        for step in &self.steps {
            // Execute step
            match step.action.execute().await {
                Ok(result) => {
                    // Record completion
                    self.completed.push(CompletedStep {
                        step: step.clone(),
                        result: result.clone(),
                    });
                }
                Err(error) => {
                    // Compensate completed steps
                    self.compensate(error).await?;
                    return Ok(SagaResult::Compensated);
                }
            }
        }

        self.state = SagaState::Completed;
        Ok(SagaResult::Success)
    }

    pub async fn compensate(&mut self, error: Error) -> Result<()> {
        self.state = SagaState::Compensating;

        // Compensate in reverse order
        for completed in self.completed.iter().rev() {
            if let Some(compensation) = &completed.step.compensation {
                compensation.compensate(&completed.result).await?;
            }
        }

        self.state = SagaState::Compensated;
        Ok(())
    }
}
```

**Workflow Integration**:
```rust
use workflow_rs::{Workflow, WorkflowEngine};

impl Saga {
    pub fn as_workflow(&self) -> Workflow {
        let mut workflow = Workflow::new(self.id.to_string());

        for step in &self.steps {
            // Add forward action
            workflow = workflow.add_step(
                step.name.clone(),
                step.action.clone()
            );

            // Add compensation
            if let Some(compensation) = &step.compensation {
                workflow = workflow.add_compensation(
                    step.name.clone(),
                    compensation.clone()
                );
            }
        }

        workflow
    }

    pub async fn execute_with_workflow(
        &self,
        engine: &WorkflowEngine
    ) -> Result<SagaResult> {
        let workflow = self.as_workflow();
        engine.execute(workflow).await?;
        Ok(SagaResult::Success)
    }
}
```

**When to Use**:
- Microservice coordination
- Long-running transactions
- Eventual consistency is acceptable
- Performance is important

**When NOT to Use**:
- Strong ACID guarantees required (use 2PC)
- Simple single-database operations (use local transactions)

