> **Unicode utilities for Rust - Correct, performant, complete**

`unicode-rs` provides a comprehensive, ergonomic API for Unicode text operations in Rust. From normalization to segmentation, case conversion to emoji handling, it makes working with Unicode text **simple and correct**.

## ⚡️ Quick Start

```toml
[dependencies]
unicode-rs = "0.1"
```

```rust
use unicode_rs::UnicodeStr;

fn main() {
    let text = "Café";

    // Normalize (handles é vs e + combining accent)
    let normalized = text.normalize(NFC);

    // Count user-perceived characters (graphemes)
    let count = text.grapheme_count(); // Not chars()!

    // Case-insensitive comparison
    let matches = "CAFÉ".eq_casefold(text);

    // Calculate display width (for terminal/UI)
    let width = text.width(); // Handles wide characters

    println!("Normalized: {}, Count: {}, Width: {}, Matches: {}",
             normalized, count, width, matches);
}
```

## ✨ Key Features

- **Normalization** - All 4 forms (NFC, NFD, NFKC, NFKD)
- **Segmentation** - Grapheme clusters, words, sentences, lines
- **Case Conversion** - Uppercase, lowercase, titlecase, foldcase
- **Bidirectional Text** - LTR/RTL detection and reordering
- **Emoji Support** - Detection, properties, transformation
- **Security** - Spoofing detection, confusable checks
- **Zero-Copy** - Lazy evaluation, borrowed slices
- **SIMD** - Accelerated ASCII fast paths
- **Streaming** - Process large files without loading into memory

## 📖 Why unicode-rs?

### The Problem

Unicode is **hard**. What looks like a single character can be:
- Multiple code points (👋🏻 = 👋 + skin tone modifier)
- Multiple representations (é = U+00E9 or e + combining accent)
- Multiple directions (mixed LTR/RTL text)
- Multiple widths (Chinese characters are 2 columns)

### The Solution

`unicode-rs` handles all the complexity, so you don't have to:

```rust
// WRONG: Counts code points
let count = "👋🏻".chars().count(); // 2 (wrong!)

// RIGHT: Counts grapheme clusters
let count = "👋🏻".grapheme_count(); // 1 (correct!)

// WRONG: Direct comparison
if "café" == "cafe\u{301}" { } // false (wrong!)

// RIGHT: Normalized comparison
if "café".eq_casefold("cafe\u{301}") { } // true (correct!)
```

## 🎯 Use Cases

### Text Processing

```rust
use unicode_rs::UnicodeStr;

// Sanitize user input
let clean = user_input
    .normalize(NFC)           // Normalize
    .trim()                   // Trim whitespace
    .to_lowercase();          // Lowercase
```

### Search Indexing

```rust
// Always normalize before indexing
let normalized = text.normalize(NFC);
let searchable = normalized.to_foldcase();
index.insert(&searchable, doc_id);
```

### Terminal Display

```rust
// Calculate display width (not bytes!)
let text = "Hello 世界";
let width = text.width(); // 11, not 13 bytes

// Truncate to width
let truncated = text.graphemes()
    .scan(0, |width, g| {
        *width += g.width();
        if *width <= 10 { Some(*g) } else { None }
    })
    .collect::<String>();
```

### Security

```rust
use unicode_rs::security;

// Detect homograph attacks
if security::is_spoofing_attempt("example.com", "еxample.com") {
    return Err(SecurityError::PossibleSpoofing);
}

// Check for normalization anomalies
if !security::is_normalized_nfc(user_input) {
    // Might be attempting to bypass validation
}
```

## 📚 Common Operations

### Normalization

```rust
use unicode_rs::{UnicodeStr, NormalizationForm};

let text = "Noe\u{308}l"; // Noël

// NFC (recommended)
let nfc = text.normalize(NormalizationForm::NFC);
assert_eq!(nfc, "Noël");

// Check if normalized
if !text.is_normalized(NormalizationForm::NFC) {
    let normalized = text.normalize(NormalizationForm::NFC);
}
```

### Grapheme Segmentation

```rust
use unicode_rs::UnicodeStr;

// Iterate user-perceived characters
for grapheme in text.graphemes() {
    println!("{}", grapheme);
}

// Count graphemes
let count = text.grapheme_count();

// Reverse (correctly!)
let reversed: String = text.graphemes().rev().collect();
```

### Word/Sentence Segmentation

```rust
use unicode_rs::UnicodeStr;

// Words
for word in text.words() {
    println!("'{}'", word);
}

// Sentences (handles abbreviations)
for sentence in text.sentences() {
    println!("'{}'", sentence.trim());
}
```

### Case Conversion

```rust
use unicode_rs::UnicodeStr;

let text = "Hello World";

// Uppercase
let upper = text.to_uppercase();

// Lowercase
let lower = text.to_lowercase();

// Case-insensitive comparison
if s1.eq_casefold(s2) {
    // Match!
}
```

### Emoji Handling

```rust
use unicode_rs::emoji::EmojiProperties;

// Detect emoji
if text.has_emoji() {
    println!("Contains emoji!");
}

// Iterate emoji
for emoji in text.emojis() {
    println!("{}", emoji);
}

// Remove skin tone modifiers
let base = emoji.remove_skin_tone();
```

## 🚀 Performance

`unicode-rs` is designed for performance:

- **Zero-Copy**: Iterators return borrowed slices
- **Lazy**: Only allocate when necessary
- **SIMD**: Accelerated ASCII fast paths (AVX2, NEON)
- **Streaming**: Process large files without loading into memory

```rust
// Zero-copy iteration (no allocation!)
for grapheme in text.graphemes() {
    // grapheme: &str (borrowed)
}

// Lazy normalization (only allocates if needed)
let normalized = text.normalize(NFC);
// Returns Cow<str> - borrowed if already normalized
```

### Benchmarks

On Intel Xeon (AVX2):

| Operation | Performance |
|-----------|-------------|
| ASCII normalization | ~5 GB/s |
| ASCII case conversion | ~6 GB/s |
| Grapheme iteration | ~500 MB/s |
| Property queries (ASCII) | ~2 GB/s |

## 🔧 Advanced Features

### Bidirectional Text

```rust
use unicode_rs::bidi::BidiProcessor;

let text = "Hello مرحبا";

// Detect direction
let direction = text.direction();

// Reorder for display
let visual = BidiProcessor::new(text).logical_to_visual();
```

### Streaming Normalization

```rust
use unicode_rs::StreamingNormalizer;

// Process large files without loading into memory
let mut normalizer = StreamingNormalizer::new(NFC);

for chunk in chunks {
    let normalized = normalizer.feed(chunk);
    process(&normalized);
}

let final = normalizer.finish();
process(&final);
```

### Security Checks

```rust
use unicode_rs::security;

// Detect spoofing attempts
if security::is_spoofing_attempt(url1, url2) {
    return Err(SecurityError::PossibleSpoofing);
}

// Check for confusable scripts
if security::has_confusable_scripts(text) {
    return Err(SecurityError::ConfusableCharacters);
}

// Strip bidi exploits
let safe = security::strip_bidi_controls(text);
```

## 📦 Feature Flags

```toml
[dependencies]
unicode-rs = { version = "0.1", features = ["simd", "streaming"] }
```

- **simd** - Enable SIMD acceleration (AVX2, NEON)
- **streaming** - Enable streaming normalization
- **embed-data** - Embed Unicode data at compile time (larger binary, faster)
- **emoji** - Emoji utilities (enabled by default)
- **security** - Security features (enabled by default)

