## Hot Reload for Development

### Use Case: Auto-Restart Development Server

When developing web services, you want the server to restart automatically when code changes.

#### Implementation with watcher-rs

```rust
use watcher_rs::Watcher;
use std::process::Command;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> watcher_rs::Result<()> {
    Watcher::new("src/")?
        .recursive(true)
        .filter_extension(["rs"])
        .debounce(std::time::Duration::from_millis(100))
        .on_change_async(|_| async move {
            println!("Code changed, restarting server...");

            // Kill existing server
            let _ = Command::new("pkill")
                .arg("-f")
                .arg("myserver")
                .status();

            // Wait a moment for graceful shutdown
            tokio::time::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(100)).await;

            // Start new server
            Command::new("cargo")
                .args(["run", "--bin", "myserver"])
                .spawn()?;

            Ok(())
        })
        .await?;

    Ok(())
}
```

#### Why watcher-rs excels

- **Fast debouncing**: 100ms debounce = quick feedback
- **Extension filtering**: Only watch `.rs` files
- **Async handlers**: Properly handle process spawning
- **Cross-platform**: Works on Linux, macOS, Windows

#### Comparison with alternatives

| Tool | Lines of Code | Debouncing | Extension Filter |
|------|--------------|------------|------------------|
| **watcher-rs** | ~15 | ✅ Built-in | ✅ Yes |
| notify | ~50+ | ❌ Manual | ❌ Manual |
| watchexec (CLI) | N/A | ✅ Yes | ⚠️ Glob-only |

### Use Case: Frontend Hot Module Replacement

Watch for frontend file changes and trigger HMR:

```rust
use watcher_rs::Watcher;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> watcher_rs::Result<()> {
    // Watch JavaScript files
    Watcher::new("src/js/")?
        .filter_extension(["js", "jsx", "ts", "tsx"])
        .debounce(std::time::Duration::from_millis(50))
        .on_change(|event| {
            println!("JS changed: {:?}", event.path);
            trigger_hmr(&event.path);
        })?
        .await?;

    // Watch CSS files
    Watcher::new("src/css/")?
        .filter_extension(["css", "scss", "sass"])
        .debounce(std::time::Duration::from_millis(50))
        .on_change(|event| {
            println!("CSS changed: {:?}", event.path);
            reload_css();
        })?
        .await?;

    Ok(())
}

fn trigger_hmr(path: &std::path::Path) {
    // Send HMR signal to dev server
    reqwest::Client::new()
        .post("http://localhost:3000/__hmr")
        .body(path.to_string_lossy().to_string())
        .send()
