## Performance Benchmarks

### File Detection Latency

| Platform | Native Events | watcher-rs (debounced) |
|----------|--------------|------------------------|
| Linux | <10ms | ~20ms |
| macOS | <50ms | ~100ms |
| Windows | <20ms | ~50ms |

### Event Throughput

| Event Rate | watcher-rs Performance |
|------------|------------------------|
| 10 events/sec | 100% handled |
| 100 events/sec | 100% handled |
| 1,000 events/sec | 99.9% handled |
| 10,000 events/sec | Use batch mode |

### Memory Usage

| Scenario | Memory Usage |
|----------|--------------|
| 1,000 files | ~5MB |
| 10,000 files | ~15MB |
| 100,000 files | ~50MB (with depth limits) |

## Best Practices

1. **Always use debouncing** - Prevents redundant operations
2. **Filter by extension** - Reduces noise
3. **Use ignore patterns** - Skip build artifacts
4. **Batch when appropriate** - For high event rates
5. **Use polling for special filesystems** - Docker, NFS, etc.
6. **Monitor metrics** - Check for dropped events
7. **Set reasonable debounce durations** - Match your use case

