## Performance Optimization

### 1. Use Zero-Copy Where Possible

```rust
// Bad: Copies data
async fn send_copy(conn: &Connection, data: Vec<u8>) -> Result<()> {
    conn.send_bytes(&data).await?;  // Copies data
    Ok(())
}

// Good: Uses Bytes (reference counted)
async fn send_zero_copy(conn: &Connection, data: Bytes) -> Result<()> {
    conn.send_bytes(data).await?;  // No copy, just Arc bump
    Ok(())
}
```

### 2. Batch Messages

```rust
// Bad: Sends one at a time
for msg in messages {
    conn.send_text(msg).await?;
}

// Good: Batches sends
conn.send_batch(messages).await?;
```

### 3. Reduce Locks

```rust
// Bad: Holds lock during iteration
async fn broadcast_bad(server: &WebSocketServer, msg: &str) {
    let conns = server.connections.lock().await;
    for conn in conns.values() {
        conn.send_text(msg).await?;  // Holds lock
    }
}

// Good: Clone IDs, release lock
async fn broadcast_good(server: &WebSocketServer, msg: &str) {
    let ids: Vec<_> = server.connections.lock().await
        .keys()
        .copied()
        .collect();
    // Lock released

    for id in ids {
        if let Some(conn) = server.get_connection(id).await {
            conn.send_text(msg).await?;
        }
    }
}
```

### 4. Use Tokio Spawn for Concurrent Work

```rust
// Bad: Sequential processing
server.on_text(|text: String, conn| async move {
    process_message(&text).await?;  // Blocks
    save_to_database(&text).await?; // Blocks
    Ok(())
});

// Good: Spawn tasks
server.on_text(|text: String, conn| async move {
    let text_clone = text.clone();
    tokio::spawn(async move {
        process_message(&text_clone).await;
    });

    let text_clone = text.clone();
    tokio::spawn(async move {
        save_to_database(&text_clone).await;
    });

    Ok(())
});
```

### 5. Reuse Allocations

```rust
// Bad: Allocates every time
server.on_text(|text: String, conn| async move {
    let response = format!("Echo: {}", text);  // Allocates
    conn.send_text(&response).await?;
    Ok(())
});

// Good: Reuses buffer
let mut response_buf = String::with_capacity(1024);
server.on_text(|text: String, mut conn| async move {
    response_buf.clear();
    response_buf.push_str("Echo: ");
    response_buf.push_str(&text);
    conn.send_text(&response_buf).await?;
    Ok(())
});
```

### 6. Profile and Optimize Hot Paths

```rust
// Install flamegraph
// cargo install flamegraph

// Run with profiling
// cargo flamegraph --bin websocket_server

// Look for:
// - Slow functions (tall bars)
// - Frequent allocations (wide bars)
// - Lock contention
```

